        "original_id": "be873546-fdc8-56c8-b595-aea04796ef28",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Phylica, Weldenia candida\n- Taxonomy: genera, species, Rhamnaceae\n- Places: southern Africa, Madagascar, Mascarene Islands, Île Amsterdam, Saint Helena, Tristan da Cunha, Gough Island, Mexico, Guatemala\n\nFacts:\n- Phylica is a genus of plants in the family Rhamnaceae.\n- A few Phylica species occur in other parts of southern Africa and on islands including Madagascar, the Mascarene Islands, Île Amsterdam, Saint Helena, Tristan da Cunha, and Gough Island.\n- Weldenia has a single species, Weldenia candida.\n- Weldenia candida is originally native to Mexico and Guatemala.",
